      "message": "This duplicates most of the functionality of the CarrierConfigReceiver we have in ConnectivityDiagnosticsManagerTest, except that that one seems to be more capable (e.g., it has a way to check that the broadcast matches).\n\nInstead of adding a new class here, can you move that class to a common location (e.g., frameworks/libs/net/common/testutils/devicetests/com/android/testutils/TestCarrierConfigReceiver) and use that? In order to do so, you\u0027ll have to factor out the bits of code in CarrierConfigReceiver#onReceive that are only relevant to ConnectivityDiagnosticsManagerTest (specifically, the code that checks the contents of KEY_CARRIER_CERTIFICATE_STRING_ARRAY).\n\nThose could go into a method that checks that the broadcast matches what the test expects. Something like:\n\n\n    public class TestCarrierConfigReceiver extends BroadcastReceiver {\n        ... existing code...\n\n        /**\n         * Subclasses should override this method to ensure that the\n         * broadcast matches their expectations. If this method returns\n         * false, the broadcast will be ignored. If this method throws\n         * an exception, the exception will be stored and re-thrown by\n         * waitForCarrierConfigChanged.\n         */\n        public abstract boolean matchesBroadcast(PersistableBundle configs) throws Exception {\n            return true;\n        }\n    }\n\nThe CarrierConfigReceiver in ConnectivityDiagnosticsManagerTest would then do:\n\n    private class CarrierConfigReceiver extends TestCarrierConfigReceiver {\n        @Override\n        public boolean matchesBroadcast(PersistableBundle configs) throws Exception {\n            final String[] certs \u003d carrierConfigs.getStringArray(\n                    CarrierConfigManager.KEY_CARRIER_CERTIFICATE_STRING_ARRAY);\n            ... if certs match return true, otherwise return false or throw\n        }\n    }\n\nFor this test, the matchesBroadcast method would check that if the bundle that was passed by overrideCarrierConfig was not null, that all the keys in that bundle match the keys in configs.",
